<title>KYRGYZSTAN: Kyrgyz leader hopes for oil on visit to Kazakhstan.</title>
<headline>Kyrgyz leader hopes for oil on visit to Kazakhstan.</headline>
<dateline>BISHKEK 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kyrgyz President Askar Akayev hopes to secure a one-million-tonne annual oil deal with neighbouring Kazakhstan during an official visit to the former Soviet republic, a presidential spokesman said on Monday.</p>
<p>Akayev starts his visit to the Kazakh capital Almaty on Tuesday, the spokesman said.</p>
<p>Along with a series of agreements on investment, taxation and defence, Kyrgyzstan hopes to sign a deal with Kazakhstan whereby the latter will provide the remote impoverished state bordering China with one million tonnes of crude oil annually.</p>
<p>Akayev returns to Kyrgyzstan on Wednesday.</p>
</text>
